Maintained overlays handle terminal events for Google, OpenAI
Completions/Responses and Anthropic. The adapter owns request cancellation,
consumer return and idle timeouts. Google uses the adapter-configured fetch.
OpenAI Completions uses a NextTavern-owned ordered-input module. Provider
overlays also carry typed request controls and Responses metadata.

The fixed alpha.7 performance patch also removes repeated per-delta JSON
parsing in six providers, retaining final argument parsing. Bedrock, Mistral
and Pi Messages source modules are maintained for those official differences.

The integrity-locked upstream npm archive supplies the rest of the SDK,
including the full model catalog. ORIGIN.json records its archive integrity,
source recovery, upstream hashes and the latest verified fork snapshot. The
NextTavern public repository carries the maintained source under
development/pi-ai. The separate compatibility fork still needs to receive
the current overlays and packaging metadata.
